# eWaste Hub Backend API Documentation

## 1. Overview

This document describes the backend REST APIs for the eWaste Hub project.

The API routes are defined by Spring Boot Controllers using class-level and method-level mappings, such as @RequestMapping, @GetMapping, @PostMapping, @PutMapping, and @PatchMapping.

Example:

Class-level mapping:
@RequestMapping("/api/auth")

Method-level mapping:
@PostMapping("/login")

Final endpoint:
POST /api/auth/login

The backend uses session-based authentication. After successful login, the backend stores the Spring Security context in the HTTP session. Frontend requests should include cookies using credentials: "include".

Default local test accounts are automatically created by AdminSeeder if they do not already exist:

ADMIN:
Email: admin@test.com
Password: admin123

OWNER:
Email: owner@test.com
Password: 123456

STAFF:
Email: staff@test.com
Password: 123456


==================================================
2. AUTH API
==================================================

Base path:
/api/auth

--------------------------------------------------
2.1 Register
--------------------------------------------------

Endpoint:
POST /api/auth/register

Description:
Registers a new user.

Request body:
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

Validation:
email: string, required, not blank
password: string, required, not blank

Response body:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Registration success",
  "userId": "USER_UUID",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "role": "OWNER"
}

Possible failed response:
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Email already exists",
  "userId": null,
  "email": null,
  "role": null
}


--------------------------------------------------
2.2 Login
--------------------------------------------------

Endpoint:
POST /api/auth/login

Description:
Logs in a user and creates a session.

Request body:
{
  "email": "owner@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

Response body:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login success",
  "userId": "USER_UUID",
  "email": "owner@test.com",
  "role": "OWNER"
}

Frontend example:
await fetch("/api/auth/login", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
  },
  credentials: "include",
  body: JSON.stringify({
    email: "owner@test.com",
    password: "123456"
  })
});


--------------------------------------------------
2.3 Get Current User
--------------------------------------------------

Endpoint:
GET /api/auth/me

Description:
Returns the currently authenticated user.

Success response:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Authenticated user",
  "userId": "USER_UUID",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "role": "OWNER"
}

Not authenticated response:
HTTP 401 Unauthorized

{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Not authenticated",
  "userId": null,
  "email": null,
  "role": null
}


--------------------------------------------------
2.4 Logout
--------------------------------------------------

Endpoint:
POST /api/auth/logout

Description:
Logs out the current user by invalidating the session.

Response body:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Logout success",
  "userId": null,
  "email": null,
  "role": null
}


